//! Minimal WinRT XAML bindings for the injected engine.
//!
//! Hand-written rather than generated: only the handful of interfaces the
//! styler port needs is touched, the crate builds in about a second, and every
//! IID comes from [`docs/winrt-abi.md`](docs/winrt-abi.md) (generated by
//! `tools/metadump` from the OS `.winmd` files).
//!
//! # Slot convention (this bit used to be wrong, twice)
//!
//! WinMD interfaces derive from `IInspectable`, whose three methods sit *after*
//! IUnknown, so an interface's own methods start at absolute vtable slot 6:
//!
//! ```text
//! 0 QueryInterface  1 AddRef  2 Release
//! 3 GetIids         4 GetRuntimeClassName  5 GetTrustLevel
//! 6.. first method of the interface
//! ```
//!
//! `tools/metadump` originally printed `3 + methodIndex`, which is the layout of
//! `xamlom.h`-style (IUnknown-based) interfaces only. Using those numbers
//! against a WinRT interface calls `IInspectable::GetIids` in place of the
//! intended method, which is exactly the bug that made the first probe "load" a
//! `<Grid/>` and then crash on the returned IID array
//! (`vtbl=0x4955534F9891C6BD` = the first 8 bytes of `IID_IXamlReaderStatics`).
//! The doc has been regenerated and [`ids`] carries the absolute numbers.
//!
//! # Ownership
//!
//! [`com::ComPtr`] is a *borrowed* handle (it is `Copy`, like the engine's
//! `ComPtr`): every successful call that hands back a reference is released
//! explicitly with [`com::ComPtr::release`]. Functions in [`xaml`] release every
//! temporary they create, so their return values are the only references the
//! caller owns.
//!
//! # Faults
//!
//! Every COM call that can touch XAML goes through [`com::guarded`], which wraps
//! it in the `__try/__except` shim from `src/seh_guard.c`. A fault is reported
//! as an `Err(exception_code)` instead of unwinding into Rust's frames.

pub mod com;
pub mod ids;
pub mod xaml;
